      "# Issue #22 final authority synthesis\n\nProduce a final construction scheme—or an explicit bounded discussion draft if a genuine unresolved interface choice remains—using the new owner synthesis and the two prior Judge receipts.\n\nThe owner defines the parallel workflow as an external capability exam, not repository-owned orchestration. Reconcile the prior authority accordingly.\n\nDecide:\n\n1. The exact non-normative reference workflow that may be documented without prescribing caller topology.\n2. Which existing package roles/contracts already satisfy each single-invocation seat in that workflow.\n3. Which missing package capability is genuinely pulled into construction scope. In particular, finalize the Merger role boundary after reconsideration.\n4. Whether any existing Judge, Fixer, Coder, or Reviewer contract requires modification to support the exam. Do not invent changes merely to encode orchestration.\n5. Remove or demote every prior prescription that belongs only to an external lane/queue/worktree/publication implementation, including candidate/CAS policy. Preserve only role-level input facts needed by a single invocation.\n6. Give minimal package-owned construction slices, contract acceptance criteria, Soul placement, exports/docs/tests, and explicit out-of-scope items.\n7. State whether construction can proceed directly or whether a Plan has a legitimate missing deliverable.\n\nRespect ADR 0001 and ADR 0010. The example must not become a hidden workflow engine, normative ordering law, next-role field, or package-owned stopping/retry policy. Submit exactly one verdict through `ak_judge_output`."
